# Gift trails

Each person/year route is a **gift**: puzzle content, assets, and storage keys stay in that trail.

**Shared practice** (helpers, UI shells, fix patterns) graduates to `$lib` when a second gift needs them — not by importing another trail’s internals.

| | Do | Don’t |
|--|--|--|
| Puzzle data, media, keys, trail-only UI | Keep under `src/routes/<gift>/` | |
| Fixes / patterns reused by a second gift | Move to `$lib` with a stable import | Import from `../otherGift/` or `../../otherGift/` |
| Older gifts | Leave alone unless a deliberate migrate | Patch “while you’re here” or break them via shared churn |

Copying a prior gift as a starting point is fine. Sibling imports (e.g. `lrnz26` → `gcm26/ResultFullscreen`) are not — they couple without an API.

New gifts should be technically at least as careful as the previous one (runes, safe storage, no prerender/hydration entropy). Improvements that only live in the newest trail are the cost of isolating old gifts; they are not a substitute for `$lib` when the pattern is shared.

